    {
      "id": "msg-4",
      "role": "assistant",
      "text": "All 75 checks pass now. The report lists two risks. I'll flag a fix for the height one.\n\nRisk: Near a limit: overall height limit is 15.1 mm, right at the 15.1 mm maximum, on the lid at (11.0, 105.0, 7.6). Fix ready to accept on its own: Lower the lid top to 7.4 mm (top wall 2.3 mm) for 0.2 mm height margin.\n\nI updated the enclosure lid for b-parasite 2.0, and all 75 checks pass now. Strength, drop and heat aren't tested by any check, so they need a review by hand.\n\n**What changed on the board, and what failed:**\n- **Q4 light sensor:** it moved to (1.08, 120.74) and turned 90°, so the old window was over solid lid. The sensor-window fit and clear checks failed. I moved and turned `opening_Q4` to match.\n- **U2 humidity sensor:** it moved about 5.6 mm to (17.08, 97.37), but the vent was still at the old spot. The vent fit and clear checks failed. I moved `opening_U2` onto the sensor.\n- **RST1 and SW1:** these two push buttons are new, and the lid had no openings for them. The fit and reach checks failed for both. I added `opening_RST1` and `opening_SW1`, each 4.7 × 3.0 mm.\n- **U1 antenna keep-out:** it shifted 0.08 mm, within tolerance. I updated its position anyway.\n- **Other board changes:** the outline, board thickness, mounting holes and bosses are the same in both revisions.\n\n**Two risks the checks don't block:**\n- **Overall height:** the lid is exactly at the 15.1 mm limit, with no margin. I've proposed a fix you can accept or ignore: lower the lid top to 7.4 mm. That leaves a 2.3 mm top wall and gives 0.2 mm of height margin.\n- **Thin wall between U2 and RST1:** the lid wall between the U2 vent and the RST1 button opening is 2.13 mm, only 0.13 mm over the 2 mm minimum. Both openings are placed by where the parts sit on the board, so I can't widen this wall without moving a part. I didn't propose a fix.",
      "created_at": "2026-11-18T10:45:09.322316Z",
      "model": null,
      "effort": null,
